ga-calls-forgery-experts-see-match/articleshow/123790490.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-09T21:50:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Nirmalya Dutta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123790525,imgsize-530905.cms"/></item><item><title>'Immigration fraud is not...': USCIS makes an example out of Indian-origin Rambhai Patel, sentenced for visa fraud</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123790329.cms" /&gt;Rambhai Patel, an Indian-origin man, received a 20-month jail sentence for orchestrating a visa fraud scheme involving staged armed robberies. Patel and his co-conspirator, Balwinder Singh, fabricated robberies at stores and restaurants to enable employees to fraudulently claim U visas. Patel will forfeit $850,000 and face deportation to India after serving his sentence.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/immigration-fraud-is-not-uscis-makes-an-example-out-of-indian-origin-rambhai-patel-sentenced-for-visa-fraud/articleshow/123790329.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/immigration-fraud-is-not-uscis-makes-an-example-out-of-indian-origin-rambhai-patel-sentenced-for-visa-fraud/articleshow/123790329.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-09T21:33:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123790309,imgsize-103486.cms"/></item><item><title>What's next for Nepal? Oli resigns after violent Gen Z protests, parliament torched;</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123785135.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/whats-next-for-nepal-kp-sharma-oli-resigns-after-violent-gen-z-protests-parliament-torched-question-marks-over-next-government/articleshow/123785135.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/whats-next-for-nepal-kp-sharma-oli-resigns-after-violent-gen-z-protests-parliament-torched-question-marks-over-next-government/articleshow/123785135.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-09T16:39:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123785372,imgsize-118312.cms"/></item><item><title>'Write- I'm sorry': ‘Phillies Karen’ offered $5,000 to return boy’s home run ball- on one condition</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123789826.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/write-im-sorry-phillies-karen-offered-5000-to-return-boys-home-run-ball-on-one-condition/articleshow/123789826.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/write-im-sorry-phillies-karen-offered-5000-to-return-boys-home-run-ball-on-one-condition/articleshow/123789826.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-09T21:02:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123789858,imgsize-864285.cms"/></item><item><title>'I don't see any British people': US traveller’s Heathrow video goes viral; questions why 'every worker' is Indian</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123789467.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/i-dont-see-any-british-people-us-travellers-heathrow-video-goes-viral-questions-why-every-worker-is-indian/articleshow/123789467.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/i-dont-see-any-british-people-us-travellers-heathrow-video-goes-viral-questions-why-every-worker-is-indian/articleshow/123789467.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-09T20:35:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123789502,imgsize-596210.cms"/></item><item><title>Elon Musk's one-word reaction to Scott Bessent 'browbeating' Trump official, X users say they are dying to know...</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123789404.cms" /&gt;Elon Musk's cryptic 'hmm' response to an article detailing Scott Bessent's aggressive behavior towards a Trump official has ignited speculation about a past altercation between Musk and Bessent. Rumors persist about a physical fight in the White House, with conflicting accounts of a black eye Musk sported, which he attributed to his son, but people believed Bessent did it. Bessent, however, denied causing it.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/elon-musks-one-word-reaction-to-scott-bessent-browbeating-trump-official-x-users-say-they-are-dying-to-know-/articleshow/123789404.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/elon-musks-one-word-reaction-to-scott-bessent-browbeating-trump-official-x-users-say-they-are-dying-to-know-/articleshow/123789404.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-09T20:32:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123789460,imgsize-32940.cms"/></item><item><title>Gen Z protests: Is Nepal unrest organic or ‘deep state’ regime change? Decoding Oli's ouster</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123787883.cms" /&gt;In 1971, Gil Scott-Heron warned that “the revolution will not be televised.” In Nepal, 54 years later, the revolution didn’t need to be. It was o social media, streamed, hashtagged, and VPN-routed. And when the government tried to ban the feed, Gen Z showed that revolt finds its own broadcast – with or without television, with or without permission.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/gen-z-protests-is-nepal-unrest-organic-or-deep-state-regime-change-decoding-olis-ouster/articleshow/123787883.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/gen-z-protests-is-nepal-unrest-organic-or-deep-state-regime-change-decoding-olis-ouster/articleshow/123787883.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-09T19:39:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Nirmalya Dutta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123788000,imgsize-52034.cms"/></item></channel></rss>